# Wheelspin step (CCE 06035B30, DUSA 0602CCEC). Code constants: all cars.
# DUSA, 20 Hz: an onset sets spin = rpm / 9000 (16.16); every tick
# grip = clamp(grip - spin, 0x2B85 .. 1.0) and spin -= 0x5C2.
# The grip is written fresh every tick before this step (the traction
# circle's limit / demand: CCE 06035A34, DUSA 0602CBB8), so the spin is a
# level taken off once a tick, not a loss that adds up: it keeps DUSA's size
# (CCE's rpm / 9000, 06035C38) and decays 0x5C2 x 2/3 = 0x3D7 a tick, to last
# as long as DUSA's. CCE lowered the grip floor and decays spin 1.33x faster
# in real time. Only this step reads the spin's size (06035AB6 writes
# 0xFFFF0000, no spin).
DAYTONA/RACE.BIN 06035C1A 06028000 1999 2b85           # grip floor 0.10 -> 0.17 (DUSA)
DAYTONA/RACE.BIN 06035C88 06028000 051e 03d7           # spin decay per tick (DUSA 0x5C2 x 2/3)
# Wheelspin timer (+0x176; DUSA +0x166, 0602D7E4; it gates the high-speed grip
# loss and keys the peel-out sound): set to 15 at an onset, or to the retrigger
# value when it's down to 4 or less. CCE converted the start (10 -> 15) and
# the threshold (3 -> 4) but kept DUSA's retrigger, 7; at 30 Hz 10.5, so 10.
DAYTONA/RACE.BIN 06035C74 06028000 75f8 75fb           # retrigger 15 - 8 = 7 -> 15 - 5 = 10
